@startuml deployment
title Local stack - docker compose, eleven services

skinparam shadowing false

actor Client
actor Developer

node "docker compose network" {
  node "individuals-api\nhost 8081 -> 8081" as API
  node "keycloak\nhost 8080 -> 8080" as KC
  database "keycloak-postgres\nhost 5433 -> 5432" as KCDB
  database "person-postgres\nhost 5434 -> 5432" as PSDB
  node "nexus\nhost 8083 -> 8081" as NEXUS
  node "person-service\nhost 8082 -> 8082" as PS
  node "prometheus\nhost 9090 -> 9090" as PROM
  node "alloy\nhost 12345 -> 12345" as ALLOY
  database "loki\nhost 3100 -> 3100" as LOKI
  database "tempo\nhost 3200, 4318" as TEMPO
  node "grafana\nhost 3000 -> 3000" as GRAF
}

Client --> API : POST /api/v1/auth/...
API --> KC : Admin REST API\nand OIDC token endpoint
API --> PS : POST /api/v1/users\nDELETE /api/v1/users/{id} (compensation)
PS --> PSDB : JDBC
KC --> KCDB : JDBC

PROM --> API : scrape /actuator/prometheus
PROM --> PS : scrape /actuator/prometheus
ALLOY --> API : read stdout\nvia the Docker socket
ALLOY --> PS : read stdout
ALLOY --> LOKI : push
API --> ALLOY : OTLP push /v1/traces
PS --> ALLOY : OTLP push /v1/traces
ALLOY --> TEMPO : OTLP, batched

GRAF --> PROM
GRAF --> LOKI
GRAF --> TEMPO

Developer --> NEXUS : make publish\n(person-service-client)
API ..> NEXUS : image build downloads person-service-client\nthrough host.docker.internal:8083

note right of PROM
  Prometheus pulls, the application pushes.
  That is why the app address lives in
  prometheus.yml while the Tempo address
  lives in application.yml.
end note

note bottom of NEXUS
  Not on any runtime path. person-service-client
  is published here by person-service, and the individuals-api image
  build resolves it by Maven coordinates - which
  is what keeps modules from depending on each
  other through project(":..."). make up starts
  Nexus and waits for it before that build.

  Port 8083 because the handout gives 8081
  to individuals-api, so Nexus is the one
  that moves off its own default.
end note

note right of PS
  The user aggregate (module 2). Starts only once
  person-postgres is healthy - Flyway migrates at
  start-up - and individuals-api waits for it to be
  healthy in turn.
end note

note bottom of PSDB
  person-service's database: schema person,
  and the Envers history in person_history.
end note

note right of ALLOY
  The agent for logs and traces. Logs: the
  applications write to stdout, and Docker keeps
  that in a file that dies with the container.
  Traces: the services push OTLP to Alloy, which
  batches them and passes them on to Tempo - a
  service never depends on Tempo being up.
end note

@enduml
